<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        WHOSE BEHAVIOUR THIS IS, established before changing anything.

        The Quotations list showing "Creation Date" is ODOO'S OWN DEFAULT, not
        something this repo did. `sale.view_quotation_tree`
        (sale/views/sale_order_views.xml:216) explicitly does:

            <field name="date_order" position="replace">
                <field name="create_date" string="Creation Date" optional="show"/>
            </field>

        and we ship no sale.order view at all — `grep` over addons/ returns
        nothing. The Sales *Orders* list (`sale.view_order_tree`) does not do
        the swap, so only Quotations are affected.

        WHY IT MATTERS HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE.

        For a real client the two dates are minutes apart and Odoo's choice is
        reasonable. For the demo tenant every record is created in one scripted
        run, so `create_date` is the build timestamp: seven orders all placed
        at 14:32 today, which reads as a fixture rather than a month of trading
        — worse than showing no date at all.

        So the fix belongs to the DEMO, not to core and not to clients. This
        view lives in sapian_demo_trader, which is never installed on a client
        database, so a client's Quotations list keeps Odoo's default. We are
        not second-guessing Odoo for everyone; we are making one demo readable.

        Inherited in EXTENSION mode from `sale.view_quotation_tree`, so it also
        reaches `sale.view_quotation_tree_with_onboarding` — the view the Sales
        app actually opens, which inherits that one in primary mode.
    -->
    <record id="view_quotation_tree_demo_order_date" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">sale.order.list (quotes) — demo shows the order date</field>
        <field name="model">sale.order</field>
        <field name="inherit_id" ref="sale.view_quotation_tree"/>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <field name="create_date" position="replace">
                <field name="date_order" string="Order Date" optional="show"/>
            </field>
        </field>
    </record>
</odoo>
